This study aims to determine sharp bounds for the smallest eigenvalue of a Robin problem associated with the anisotropic $p$-Laplacian:
\[
\begin{cases}
\text{div}\left(|\nabla u|^{p-2}\u\right)=\lambda p|u|^{p-2}u & \text{in}\;\;\Omega,\\
u=0 & \text{at}\;\;\partial\Omega_1,\\
\frac{\partial u}{\partial\nu}+p|u|^{p-2}u=0 & \text{at}\;\;\partial\Omega_0,
\end{cases}
\]
where $\Omega\subset\mathbb{R}^N$ is a bounded region with a Lipschitz boundary partitioned into two disjoint components, $\Omega_1$ (compact) and $\Omega_1=\emptyset$, such that $\overline{\Omega_1}\subset\Omega$; $\nu$ indicates the outward unit normal, and $\Omega_0$ supports a portion of the Robin boundary condition.

Key findings reveal that for any domain $\Omega$ containing a fixed reference domain $\Omega_0$ with $\partial\Omega_1=\partial\Omega$, the eigenfunction $u$ corresponds to the first Robin eigenvalue can be selected within the Sobolev space $W^{1,p}
